# Naming

## Generic

- Components: `PascalCase` name; file is `<Name>.component.tsx` exporting `<Name>` (`Header.component.tsx` → `Header`). Pages: `<Name>.page.tsx` exporting `<Name>Page` (`Auth.page.tsx` → `AuthPage`). One component per file.
- Hooks: `use*` prefix for any function that calls other hooks (`useViewModel`, `useDebounce`). Hook files are `camelCase` (`useViewModel.ts`); barrel-export them named.
- Utilities and helpers: `camelCase` for functions and files (`formatDate.ts`, `export function formatDate`).
- Constants: `UPPER_SNAKE_CASE` for true scalar constants (`PHONE_PATTERN`, `MAX_RETRIES`).
- Files by role (slice layers): `*.component.tsx` / `*.component.m.css` (UI), `*.vm.ts` (view-model class `XxxViewModel`), `*.interactor.ts` (use-case), `*.api.ts` (API class), `*.schema.ts` (Zod), `*.interface.ts` (domain interface), `*.page.tsx` / `*.page.m.css` / `*.page.skeleton.tsx` (pages), `*.config.ts`, `*.test.ts` / `*.test.tsx`, `*.types.ts`, `*.mock.ts`. Keep suffixes consistent — the toolchain relies on them.
- Boolean props and variables: prefix with `is`/`has`/`should`/`can` (`isCreateOtpPending`, `isOpened`); avoid negated names (`isNotLoading` — flip the polarity instead).
- Event handlers: `on*` for props (`onSubmit`, `onChange`), `handle*` for internal handlers (`handleSubmit`, `handleChange`). Don't mix the two within one component.

## Stack-specific

- Types and interfaces: Hungarian notation — `I` prefix for interfaces (`IPhone`, `IUser`), `T` prefix for type aliases (`TPhoneFormInputValues`, `TDestroyableViewModel`). The `type` vs `interface` choice is covered in `engineering/typescript`.
- Enums: Hungarian notation — `E` prefix (`EField`, `EUserRole`). Form field names follow Auth: `export enum EField { PHONE = 'phone' }`. Prefer `as const` objects + union types otherwise (see `engineering/typescript`).
- Static arrays and objects: `UPPER_SNAKE_CASE` (CONSTANT_CASE) — `PHONE_PATTERN`, `DEFAULT_HEADERS`.
- Configs: `PascalCase` with Hungarian `C` prefix (`CAppRouting`, `CAppConfig`). Config values/objects live in the `config` segment; keep `*.config.ts` file suffix.
- Slices: PascalCase directories matching the export (`Auth`, `Header`, `NotFoundError`) — not kebab-case.
- Segments (modules): canonical `presentation`, `model`, `data`, `domain`; optional `lib`, `config`, `constants`. Do not use `ui/` or `api/`. Widgets stay flat until they outgrow one component + VM (see `architecture/segments`). Pure helpers live in `~shared/lib` or the feature's `lib`.
- View-models: class `<Name>ViewModel` in `<Name>.vm.ts`, colocated with the component. Interactors: class `<Name>Interactor` in `model/`. API: class `<Name>Api` in `data/`.
- Generated code keeps its own naming: Kubb output is read-only (see `stack/general`); don't rename generated files or re-export them under hand-made names.
